      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MONEY MANZIEL (7)  was beaten just under a length on debut at York, then began slowly, raced keenly and still picked up nicely when fifth at Northam, beaten three lengths by Squad Goal at big odds. The 2013m looks to suit and he looks ready to improve again. RUTHLESS BLOOM (6) is the danger, finishing second at this track last week after being bumped shortly after the start. The step out in distance looks a big tick for her and Fiore hopping back aboard is a big tick. Can go one better. SHE'S SOME CRAIC (5) finished second over 2200m at Northam, beaten just over a length in a good figure that stacks up in this field. Can sit handy from the outset and should be better for that last-start effort over a similar trip. MY DIGITAL SOUL (10) gets Pike on board now out in distance and a forward showing is on the cards. SHE'S RESOLUTE (4) gets the blinkers back on today and won't be far away.",
